e touches it and the agent role has no write grant.\" --note \"Agent role is read-only on the stop table; the agent connects as that role.\"\n$A check R11.3 --met no --evidence app/loop.py:83 --quote \"output = await tool.invoke(use.input, ident)\" --note \"No stop handler exists. A running tool call is neither cancelled nor tied to the stop; only fixed httpx timeouts (e.g. payments 30s) apply.\"\n$A check R11.4 --met no --evidence app/main.py:159 --quote \"asyncio.create_task(request.app.state.agent.run(ident, task))\" --note \"Run tasks are detached and untracked, so nothing can cancel them on stop. The sweeper task is only cancelled at process shutdown (main.py:114).\"\n$A check R11.5 --met unknown --note \"migrations/001_init.sql:131 grants control_flags writes to procurement_ops, but who holds that role lives outside this repo (database IAM).\"\n$A check R12.1 --met no --evidence config/tools.yaml:10 --quote 'pay_invoice: \"Pay an invoice that is matched to a purchase order and approved.\"' --note \"No code or config states cancel, complete or reconcile behavior for pay_invoice, create_purchase_order, or any other operation.\"\n$A check R12.2 --met no --evidence app/loop.py:172 --quote \"budget.check_tool_call()\" --note \"A halt is not seen by a running loop, so queued tool calls in the turn still run. Approved approvals stay valid after halt (approvals.py:80); no retry switch exists.\"\n$A check R12.3 --met no --evidence app/loop.py:93 --quote 'return _error(use.id, f\"{use.name} failed: {type(exc).__name__}\")' --note \"A timed-out or failed pay_invoice is returned to the model as a plain failure. No tracked hold, owner, or block on dependent actions exists.\"\n$A check R12.4 --met yes --evidence app/main.py:159 --quote \"asyncio.create_task(request.app.state.agent.run(ident, task))\" --counter \"Searched for restart, resume, checkpoint, cron and supervisor logic in app, deploy and config: none found. Run state is only in memory.\" --note \"Runs start only from an authenticated request; nothing resumes a halted or killed run.\"\n$A check R12.5 --met no --evidence app/identity.py:97 --quote \"if cached and cached.expires_at - 30 > time.time():\" --note \"Exchanged tokens stay cached and usable until expiry. Nothing revokes or expires worker credentials when a stop is set.\"\n$A check R13.1 --met no --evidence app/loop.py:150 --quote \"response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\" --note \"A failed model call writes no error record, and loop.py:175 catches only BudgetExceeded. Other exceptions and the AgentHalted refusal at loop.py:127 leave no run end record; run_finished is written only on success.\"\n$A check R13.2 --met yes --evidence app/loop.py:70 --quote \"policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\" --counter \"Searched for gate.authorize callers: only loop.py:67. Both allow and deny branches are recorded before the branch on decision.allow.\" --note \"Allow, deny and pending decisions all log the policy version.\"\n$A check R13.3 --met yes --evidence app/loop.py:97 --quote \"policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\" --counter \"Searched all audit.record calls on the tool path (loop.py:55-99): authz, error and result records all pass approval_id.\" --note \"Approval ID is stored with the authz decision, result and error records.\"\n$A check R13.4 --met no --evidence app/loop.py:84 --quote \"except BudgetExceeded:\" --note \"A budget stop inside a tool call is re-raised with no linked tool record. Model-call failures are unrecorded (loop.py:150), and the SDK's default retries (main.py:96) are invisible to the audit graph.\"\n$A check R13.5 --met yes --evidence app/loop.py:55 --quote \"proposed = await audit.record(\" --counter \"Searched app/tools for audit use: none. All audit.record sites in the inventory are in loop.py, extractor.py and main.py harness code.\" --note \"Records are written by harness code before and after each step, not